# Frozen pre-regeneration baseline (Stage 2a). Byte-identical copies of the
# eight files in data/INPUTS.sha256, kept so nothing in Stage 2a can destroy
# the only record of what the current manuscript draft reports. Verify with
# `cd data/baseline_frozen && shasum -a 256 -c INPUTS.sha256`.
data/baseline_frozen/

# Large data files — regenerate by running Notebook 1
# (comment out these lines if you want to track them in git)
data/processed/DATA_all.json

# Synthetic corpora. Each is ~200 MB and regenerable on demand from the seed,
# configuration and commit recorded in its own runmeta.json:
#     cd src && python corpus.py <label>
# The PROVENANCE is tracked and the data are not: runmeta.json, the validity
# rejections and the pLCA groupings are small and stay in git, and
# data/INPUTS.sha256 pins the checksums of the large files so any copy can be
# proven genuine.
data/processed/corpus_*/values.parquet
data/processed/corpus_*/metrics.parquet
data/processed/corpus_*/parents.json.gz
# The two DERIVED replay caches, added in Stages 2c and 2e and not covered by
# this rule until Stage 2f. Both are rebuilt from values.parquet by replaying
# the generator -- `corpus.rebuild_parents` and `corpus.rebuild_mode_labels`,
# which verify the replay against those values element by element -- so they
# are data and not provenance, and the same argument that excludes the corpus
# excludes them. Together they are 6.6 MB per corpus, re-stored whole on every
# commit that touches them, in a repository whose history reached 2.5 GB in
# Stage 2e. A clean clone has no corpus at all and regenerates, so nothing is
# lost by not shipping a cache of it.
#
# corpus_2026-09-19's pair was committed before this rule existed and is
# untracked here, because Stage 2f created that corpus and so it is this
# stage's own mess. corpus_2026-09-15b's pair is ALSO tracked, from Stages 2c
# and 2e, and STAYS so: gitignore does not untrack a tracked file, and removing
# something an earlier stage deliberately committed is a change to the
# deposit's contents that belongs to Stage 4 rather than here.
data/processed/corpus_*/parents_spec.json.gz
data/processed/corpus_*/mode_labels.parquet

# Nested git repo (cloned GitHub copy — not needed here)
CompareUQMethods/

# Void/scratch notebooks
notebooks/VOID_*
notebooks/_SCRATCHPAD.ipynb
notebooks/CompareUQMethods_backup.ipynb

# Reference PDFs and third-party datasets (copyrighted publisher files,
# large supplementary data). Kept locally for consultation, never committed
# to this public repository.
refs/

# Manuscript drafts. Kept local: the working .docx carries unresolved comments
# from named third parties, and this repository is public and Zenodo-archived.
# Remove this rule only for a clean copy with comments resolved and accepted.
outputs/manuscript/

# Derived mode-count caches (audits/stage2a3/q3). Rebuilt from the corpus.
outputs/tables/stage2a3/CACHE_modality_*.npz

# Audit tables. The scripts under audits/ rewrite these on demand, and a script
# is a better record of a measurement than the CSV it produces. 98 of these were
# tracked and deleted on 2026-09-15; they are not tracked again.
outputs/tables/audits/
